---
description: |
  Normalizes a Cloudflare Logpush record to OCSF.

  ```tql
  from_file "s3://example-logpush/http_requests/**/*.log.gz" {
    decompress_gzip
    read_ndjson
  }
  cloudflare::ocsf::normalize
  ```

  The operator maps HTTP requests and firewall events to OCSF HTTP Activity
  and audit logs to OCSF API Activity. Whatever has no OCSF attribute remains
  under `unmapped`.

  Firewall events repeat a request once per matched rule and share its Ray ID
  in `metadata.correlation_uid`, so count requests on
  `metadata.log_name == "http_requests"`.
args:
  positional:
    - name: cloudflare
      description: The structured Cloudflare Logpush record.
      type: field
      default: this
  named:
    - name: into
      description: The field that receives the OCSF event.
      type: field
      default: this
---

$into.cloudflare = $cloudflare
cloudflare::ocsf::map $into.cloudflare, $into.ocsf
$into = $into.ocsf
